{"title":"Minimum Number Of Food Buckets To Feed The Hamsters","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"You are given a 0-indexed string hamsters where hamsters[i] is either:\n\n'H' indicating that there is a hamster at index i, or\n'.' indicating that index i is empty.\n\nYou will add some number of food buckets at the empty indices in order to feed the hamsters. A hamster can be fed if there is at least one food bucket to its left or to its right. More formally, a hamster at index i can be fed if you place a food bucket at index i - 1 and/or at index i + 1.\nReturn the minimum number of food buckets you should place at empty indices to feed all the hamsters or -1 if it is impossible to feed all of them.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: hamsters = \"H..H\"\nOutput: 2\n```\n\nWe place two food buckets at indices 1 and 2.\nIt can be shown that if we place only one food bucket, one of the hamsters will not be fed.\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: hamsters = \".H.H.\"\nOutput: 1\n```\n\nWe place one food bucket at index 2.\n\n### Example 3\n\n```text\nInput: hamsters = \".HHH.\"\nOutput: -1\n```\n\nIf we place a food bucket at every empty index, the hamster at index 2 will not be able to eat.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= hamsters.length <= 10^5\n- hamsters[i] is either'H' or '.'.\n\n## Output Contract\n\nReturn the minimum bucket count, or -1 when feeding every hamster is impossible.","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def minimumBuckets(self, hamsters: str) -> int:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().minimumBuckets","parameters":[{"name":"hamsters","type":"str"}],"returnType":"int","tests":[{"input":["."],"expected":0},{"input":["..."],"expected":0},{"input":[{"$json":"eJztwTEBAAAMAqAuBjCH/ROtxg4gBQAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAL5aDqn5NTk=","bytes":100002}],"expected":1},{"input":["..........................................................H"],"expected